# Kept out of the build context. Short list, and every line earns its place:
# without this file `COPY . .` in the builder stage pulls the whole working
# directory in, and two of these end up inside the shipped image: Next copies
# .env into .next/standalone, so `docker run <image> cat .env` prints the
# Fortnox secrets and the session key.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed inside the image. The host tree is built for this machine, and
# copying it over the container's is how you get a native module that loads
# on your laptop and not in the container.
node_modules
.next
src/lib/generated
*.tsbuildinfo

# Section financial data: real account numbers and member-identifying rows.
# No more welcome in an image than in git history.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
!**/__fixtures__/*.csv

# Nothing the build reads
.git
.claude
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

# The sibling intakt clone. Its own build, never part of this image.
/intakt
